    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0379" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg332"/>

                <head>250. Telegram 796 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d250-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-09-28">September 28, 1955, 10
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d250-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d250-1"/>
                <p>796. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>Department’s unnumbered Niact September 28 correcting text Deptel 798 not
                    received until 5 p.m. Geneva time. As will be seen from report today’s meeting
                    (Mytel 795, paragraph 6) I used phraseology “accounting for US personnel.”
                    Although I was bothered by omission of “military”, there was no time for
                    confirmation. Believe I was successful in skirting around subject and I can pick
                    up matter at next meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
